  {
   "type": "Feature",
   "properties": {
    "name": "Euphrates (Purattum)",
    "kind": "river",
    "ancient": true,
    "note": "Upper and middle course close to the modern river (Mari sat ~2 km from the channel). Below Sippar this follows the reconstructed Old Babylonian main channel (Kutha-Kish-Nippur-Isin-Shuruppak-Uruk-Ur), which lies east of today's river; after Hammurabi's reign the Euphrates shifted west and many southern cities lost their water. Re-dredged by Hammurabi's year-33 canal 'Hammurabi-nuhush-nishi' (route uncertain) supplying Nippur, Isin, Uruk, Larsa, Ur and Eridu. Lower course into the head of the Gulf is schematic."
   },
